(R) ROBBINS 1955  --  correct statement:
    sqrt(2 pi n) (n/e)^n e^{1/(12n+1)} < n! < sqrt(2 pi n) (n/e)^n e^{1/(12n)}
    equivalently  1/(12n+1) < d(n) < 1/(12n),
    d(n) := ln n! - (1/2)ln(2 pi n) - n ln n + n.
==============================================================================
  checked 2006 values of n (dense 1..2000 + sparse to 10^8): 0 violations
  smallest lower margin d-1/(12n+1): 6.94444e-19 at n=100000000
  smallest upper margin 1/(12n)-d : 2.77778e-27 at n=100000000

