(F) FGKP95 THEOREM 7.  theta(n) defined by
    (1/2)e^n = sum_{m=0}^{n-1} n^m/m!  +  theta(n) n^n/n! ,
    claim: theta(n) = 1/3 + 4/(135(n+k(n))),  k(n) in [2/21, 8/45], all n>=0,
    i.e. 1/3 + 4/(135(n+8/45)) <= theta(n) <= 1/3 + 4/(135(n+2/21)).
==============================================================================

