(L) LEMMA 1:  Q(n) = n! e^n/(2 n^n) - theta(n).
    Referee re-derivation:  Q(n) = sum_{j=0}^{n-1} prod_{i=1}^j (1-i/n),
    term_j = (n-1)!/((n-1-j)! n^j);  m := n-1-j  gives
       Q(n) = ((n-1)!/n^{n-1}) sum_{m=0}^{n-1} n^m/m!  =  (n!/n^n) S(n),
    S(n) := sum_{m=0}^{n-1} n^m/m!  [= FGKP95 eq. (1.4) verbatim].
    With S(n) = e^n/2 - theta(n) n^n/n!  (the theta definition) this IS the
    stated identity.  Both steps checked below.
==============================================================================

